<Routines>
<Routine Name="EnableInFalse" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[EnableInFalse]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[OTU(Out_GL_Ch_O.LockUnlockEn)OTU(Out_Ch_RunRdy);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="Logic" Type="RLL">
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Intialize Timers
LockFbkTmr.Pre setup is configured for system Close/Lock response and may be system size and device locking time dependent.
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOVE(500,StartupTmr.PRE)MOVE(500,LockTmr.PRE)MOVE(500,UnlockTmr.PRE)MOVE(Cfg_LockFbkTime,LockFbkTmr.PRE);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Intialize Sequence on loss of Run Mode OR First Scan
250ms was tested minimum]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIO(S:FS) XIC(Inp_ModuleName_I.RunMode) TON(StartupTmr,?,?) ,[XIO(StartupTmr.DN) ,XIO(Inp_ModuleName_I.RunMode) ] MOVE(0,LockSequence) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Initialize
Do not send GuardLink Lock/Unlock commands until 500ms into RunMode]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQ(LockSequence,0)XIC(Inp_ModuleName_I.RunMode)XIC(StartupTmr.DN)[XIO(Inp_UnlkCmd) MOVE(200,LockSequence) ,XIC(Inp_UnlkCmd) MOVE(500,LockSequence) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Unlocked
Goto Lock Command when loss of Unlock Command or a new Lock Request
Goto Unlock Command if a new Unlock Request]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQ(LockSequence,100)[[XIO(Inp_UnlkCmd) ,XIC(Inp_LkReqNew) ] MOVE(200,LockSequence) ,XIC(Inp_UnlkCmd) XIC(Inp_UnlkReqNew) MOVE(500,LockSequence) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Lock Command
Turn on LockUnlockEn and command the standard task to issue a lock command.
350ms was tested minimum effective signal]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQ(LockSequence,200)[OTL(Out_GL_Ch_O.LockUnlockEn) OTE(Out_LockCmdStd) TON(LockTmr,?,?) ,XIC(LockTmr.DN) OTU(Out_GL_Ch_O.LockUnlockEn) MOVE(300,LockSequence) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Lock Command GD Open
Timers allows time to receive closed/locked feedback, else return to Unlocked
LockFbkTmr.Pre setup is configured for system Close/Lock response and may be system size and device locking time dependent.
Goto Closed/Lock on I.Status
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQ(LockSequence,300)[TON(LockFbkTmr,?,?) XIC(LockFbkTmr.DN) MOVE(100,LockSequence) ,XIC(Inp_GL_Ch_I.Status) MOVE(400,LockSequence) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Closed and Locked ]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQ(LockSequence,400)[OTE(Closed_Lock_State) ,XIC(Inp_UnlkCmd) MOVE(500,LockSequence) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Unlock Command
350ms was tested minimum]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQ(LockSequence,500)[OTL(Out_GL_Ch_O.LockUnlockEn) OTE(Out_UnLockCmdStd) TON(UnlockTmr,?,?) ,XIC(UnlockTmr.DN) XIO(Inp_GL_Ch_I.Status) OTU(Out_GL_Ch_O.LockUnlockEn) MOVE(100,LockSequence) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Status for use in Safety Functions
Verify the detected device count is equal to the expected number.
Must be in closed and lock state
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Inp_GL_Ch_I.Status)EQ(Inp_GL_Ch_I.DeviceCount,Cfg_Channel_DeviceCount)XIC(Closed_Lock_State)OTE(Out_Ch_RunRdy);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="9" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Status for display on AOI ]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Out_GL_Ch_O.LockUnlockEn)OTE(Out_LockUnlockEn_Sts);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
</Routines>
